==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|nobilité}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|nobilitas}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/noʊˈbɪlɪti/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/nəʊˈbɪlɪti/|/nəˈbɪlɪti/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪlɪti}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|nobilities}}

# A [[noble]] or privileged social class, historically accompanied by a [[hereditary]] title; [[aristocracy]].
#: {{syn|en|aristocracy|upper class}}
#: {{ant|en|plebeian}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The quality of being [[noble]].
#: {{syn|en|aristocracy|nobleness}}
#: {{ant|en|meanness|ignobility}}

